I'm going to reverse your order here to make the
answer easier to understand/write.

 > it's a game which lends itself fine to C alone.

If that were the case the existing code would
presumably be straightforward, well organized,
modular, loosely coupled, easily maintainable, and
easy to read. It is none of those things (and I've
programmed in C since 1983, so I have the right to
comment).

 > Why OO?>

_Lots_ of NetHack is "standard behavior" plus
"specialized behavior", monsters, grid cells,
objects, and so on, and in several levels of
increasing specialization. This cries out for the
support for hierarchical code inheritance that OOs
provide, to eliminate redundant code, and improve
maintainablity and extensibility.

